tion should raise an error in the case it can't withdrawal all the funds invested from the used contracts"},"getRoleAdmin(bytes32)":{"details":"Returns the admin role that controls `role`. See {grantRole} and {revokeRole}. To change a role's admin, use {_setRoleAdmin}."},"getUnused()":{"returns":{"_0":"unused amount of assets"}},"grantRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Grants `role` to `account`. If `account` had not been already granted `role`, emits a {RoleGranted} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role."},"hasRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Returns `true` if `account` has been granted `role`."},"migrateFunds(address,address[],bool,bool)":{"details":"SHOULD only be called by the GOVERNOR. Emits {FundsMigrated}"},"purchaseOption(uint256,uint256)":{"params":{"_amount":"Amount of puts/calls to purchase. Returns bool to indicate if put/call purchase went through sucessfully.","_strikeIndex":"Strike index for current epoch."}},"renounceRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from the calling account. Roles are often managed via {grantRole} and {revokeRole}: this function's purpose is to provide a mechanism for accounts to lose their privileges if they are compromised (such as when a trusted device is misplaced). If the calling account had been revoked `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must be `account`."},"repay()":{"details":"SHOULD only be called by the strategistsSHOULD call a very specific method on the vault \"depositProfits\"SHOULD emit event Repay(vault, asset, amount)"},"revokeRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from `account`. If `account` had been granted `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role."},"sell2CrvForBase(uint256,address,uint256,uint256)":{"params":{"_amount":"The amount of 2CRV to sell","_minAssetAmount":"The minimum amount of base asset to receive Returns the amount of base asset","_minStableAmount":"The minimum amount of `_stableToken` to get when swapping 2CRV","_stableToken":"The address of the stable token to receive when removing 2CRV lp"}},"sellBaseFor2Crv(uint256,address,uint256,uint256)":{"params":{"_baseAmount":"The amount of base asset to sell","_min2CrvAmount":"The minimum amount of 2CRV to receive Returns the amount of 2CRV tokens","_minStableAmount":"The minimum amount of `_stableToken` to get when swapping base","_stableToken":"The address of the stable token that will be used as intermediary to get 2CRV"}},"sellUSDCForAsset(uint256)":{"params":{"_minAssetOutputFromUSDCSwap":"Minimum asset output from swapping USDC."}},"setVault(address)":{"details":"Attaches `_vault` to this strategy. Only a strategist can attach vault and can only happen once. This method is used over the constructor to prevent circular dependency. Should revert with error if vault is already attached. Invoke `whitelistStrategy` on vault after calling this to whitelist this strategy for the vault to be able to pull assets and perform other restricted actions. Emits {VaultSet}."},"settleEpoch(uint256,uint256[])":{"params":{"_ssovEpoch":"The SSOV epoch to settle.","_ssovStrikes":"The SSOV strike indexes to settle."}},"supportsInterface(bytes4)":{"details":"See {IERC165-supportsInterface}."},"swap2CRVBalanceForUSDC(uint256)":{"params":{"_minUSDCOutput":"Minimum USDC output from selling 2crv."}},"withdrawEpoch(uint256,uint256[])":{"params":{"_epoch":"The SSOV epoch to withdraw from.","_strikes":"The SSOV strikes."}}},"version":1},"userdoc":{"events":{"Borrow(address,uint256,address,address)":{"notice":"Emitted when borrowing assets from the underlying vault."},"FundsMigrated(address)":{"notice":"Emitted when migrating funds (ex in case of an emergency)."},"Repay(address,uint256,address,address)":{"notice":"Emitted when closing the strategy."},"VaultDetached(address,address)":{"notice":"Emitted when detaching the vault."},"VaultSet(address,address)":{"notice":"Emitted when attaching the vault."}},"kind":"user","methods":{"SSOV()":{"notice":"SSOV contract"},"SSOVViewer()":{"notice":"SSOV Viewer contract"},"asset()":{"notice":"Returns the base erc20 asset for the strategy. Assumption: For now, strategies only accept one base asset at the time (i.e the same strat cannot invest ETH and DPX ony one or the other)."},"borrow(uint256)":{"notice":"Borrow base assets from the vault. This will borrow the required `_amount` in base assets from the vault."},"depositSSOV(uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Deposits funds to SSOV at desired strike price."},"depositSSOVMultiple(uint256[],uint256[])":{"notice":"Deposits funds to SSOV at multiple desired strike prices."},"detach()":{"notice":"Detaches the strategy. For some reason we might want to detach the strat from the vault, this function should close all open positions, repay the vault and remove itself from the vault whitelist. Reverts if pending settlements or unable to withdraw every deposit after calling `repay`. This is to ensure that the Strategy only detaches if everything is settled and deposited assets are repaid to vault. Make sure to invoke `removeStrategyFromWhitelist` on previously detached vault after detaching."},"getUnused()":{"notice":"Returns the current unused assets in the strategy."},"getVault()":{"notice":"Returns the vault attached to strategy. Should revert with error if vault is not attached."},"migrateFunds(address,address[],bool,bool)":{"notice":"Migrates funds to specified address `_to`."},"purchaseOption(uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Buys options from Dopex SSOV."},"repay()":{"notice":"Returns the funds back to the vault."},"router()":{"notice":"ssov v3 router"},"sell2CrvForBase(uint256,address,uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Sells 2CRV for the base asset"},"sellBaseFor2Crv(uint256,address,uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Sells the base asset for 2CRV"},"sellUSDCForAsset(uint256)":{"notice":"Sells USDC balance for the asset token"},"settleEpoch(uint256,uint256[])":{"notice":"Settles the SSOV epoch."},"s